Cemetery
Midland Cemetery occupies one of the nicest pieces of land in the city, atop the rolling bluffs of the west bank. The cemetery dates back to the time of the original St. Michael's building, and some of the gravestones are two hundred years old. Many of the stones have been etched with ugly graffiti, like "PAP," a derogatory term for Catholics, and "JEEBOO," an epithet for any nonmember of the Church. Near the main gate of the cemetery, to the west, the land has been bulldozed but is now overgrown with weeds, indicating a construction project that was begun but then abandoned. Other gates lie to the south, southwest, and northwest.

Main & Church
You are at the corner of bustling Main Street and quiet Church Street. There are nondescript buildings on the northwestern and southwestern corners. A conventional apartment building occupies the southeast corner, and an entrance to Midland Cemetery forms the fourth corner. A particularly blockish Indoor City towers over Church Street south of here.

You hear shots from a nearby building. Seconds later, Security Police carry a bleeding man out of the building and into a waiting skyvan. A woman runs out of the building, screaming. One of the officers kicks her in the stomach and clubs her across the skull as she falls. Nonchalantly, the policeman climbs into the skyvan, which rises away.

