Perelman walks into the office and spots the active light on your communication unit immediately. "Hello, PRISM," he says, sitting down at his desk. "It looks like you beat me here. Give me a moment, please." He begins quickly jotting a few notes onto a pad.

Perelman looks up. "PRISM, several of my colleagues and I have finished viewing the recordings that you made, and everyone agreed that 2051, '61, and '71 all looked disturbing. But there wasn't anything interesting from 2081. Perhaps things turn around. Maybe you could collect some more data, make some more recordings, and then report back to us. Well, I've got to run, but I'll talk to you later." He leaves the room.

